---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith("/") ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About - NV Studio Design"
  description="About NV Studio Design &mdash; a residential architecture and interior design practice based in the Greater Toronto Area."
>
  <section id="one">
    <div class="inner">
      <header class="major">
        <h1>About NV Studio Design</h1>
      </header>

      <p>
        NV Studio Design is a residential architecture and interior design
        practice based in the Greater Toronto Area. We work on custom
        homes, renovations, additions, and secondary suites across the
        GTA and Ontario.
      </p>
      <p>
        The studio exists for a specific reason: to design houses &mdash;
        and nothing else. Commercial, institutional, and large-scale
        developments are handled better by practices that specialise in
        them. Houses need a different kind of attention: to the family
        that will live there, to the existing neighbourhood, to a lot
        that&rsquo;s often constrained, and to the municipal rules that
        govern all of it.
      </p>

      <!--
        The biography below is intentionally left in {{ placeholder }} form.
        The studio lead should fill these in via docs/content-questionnaire.md.
        Do not fabricate credentials, years, or education.
      -->
      <h2>Nikolay Vagano &mdash; Principal</h2>
      <p>
        {"{{ bio_paragraph — 3 to 5 sentences: where Nikolay is from, how he came to residential architecture, what he cares about in the work. Fill from content questionnaire. }}"}
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Credentials:</strong>
        {"{{ credentials — e.g. OAA licensed architect, BCIN-qualified designer, RAIC member. Leave blank until confirmed. }}"}
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Education:</strong>
        {"{{ education — school, degree, year. Leave blank if not public. }}"}
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Years in practice:</strong>
        {"{{ years_in_practice — e.g. \"since 2015\" or \"over 10 years\". }}"}
      </p>

      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>One integrated process.</strong> Architectural design,
          interior design, and permits are a single engagement, not three
          separate ones. Decisions made in one feed directly into the others.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Residential only.</strong> Everything in the portfolio
          is a home. That&rsquo;s a choice, not an accident.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A small practice.</strong>
          {"{{ team_note — solo practice, or names/roles of collaborators. }}"}
          Clients work directly with the person designing the house, not
          with a project manager relaying messages.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Clear scope, honest timelines.</strong> We write the
          scope down, we name the deliverables, and we don&rsquo;t promise
          dates we can&rsquo;t hit.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Philosophy, briefly</h2>
      <p>
        Good residential architecture is usually specific rather than
        striking. A house is shaped by the people who will live in it,
        the orientation of the lot, a budget, and a by-law &mdash; and a
        good design works all of those out quietly without needing to
        shout about it. That&rsquo;s the standard we hold the work to.
      </p>

      <h2>Where we work</h2>
      <p>
        Based in {"{{ studio_location — public address or \"Greater Toronto Area\" }}"}.
        Most projects are in Toronto and the surrounding GTA; we take on
        work elsewhere in Ontario when the site is interesting and the
        brief is right.
      </p>

      <ul class="actions">
        <li><a href={`${baseUrl}portfolio`} class="button">See Our Work</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${baseUrl}contact`} class="button primary">Book a Consultation</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
